(Measurements for understanding the pace of AI development inside frontier labs) Tj T*
(Anthropic \(Anthropic Institute\), published 17 September 2026) Tj T*
(Source: https://www.anthropic.com/institute/measuring-pace-of-ai-development) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(AI systems are becoming exponentially more powerful and have begun to automate more of the) Tj T*
(process of building themselves. As the world considers slowing the pace of frontier AI) Tj T*
(development, the public needs more information.) Tj T*
(In this post, we lay out measurement tools that can illuminate three critical aspects of AI) Tj T*
(development:) Tj T*
(The extent to which AI is building the next version of itself, as opposed to being built by) Tj T*
(humans) Tj T*
(Our ability to oversee and intervene in actions that AI agents take on Anthropic's systems) Tj T*
(The resources that power the development of more capable models) Tj T*
(We also provide a snapshot of these metrics from inside Anthropic. It's important to note that) Tj T*
(we would expect these numbers to shift if there were coordination on pacing the frontier, as) Tj T*
(called for by Anthropic CEO Dario Amodei. We plan to embed independent third-party evaluators) Tj T*
(from multiple organizations at Anthropic, and give them access to internal processes, systems,) Tj T*
(and data comparable to what internal risk assessment teams have. These third parties will) Tj T*
(verify safety practices, report incidents, and monitor key metrics such as the ones in this) Tj T*
(piece.) Tj T*
(We are reporting these measurements because they give the public, third parties, and) Tj T*
(governments better visibility into the pace of AI development inside frontier labs. For each) Tj T*
(measurement, we describe what we measured, what the measurement showed, and what it would take) Tj T*
(to publish these measurements regularly in a form others can verify. We share methodological) Tj T*
(details in the Appendix.) Tj T*
(Reasons to track these measurements) Tj T*
(The measurements in this piece are focused on how models are built. By better understanding the) Tj T*
(production process of models, we have a better chance of correlating model inputs, like) Tj T*
(compute, with model outputs, like capabilities. They complement capability evaluations, which) Tj T*
(measure what models can do. We publish those separately through our Responsible Scaling Policy) Tj T*
(\(RSP\) risk reports, which include evidence on how much our models are accelerating AI R&D. In) Tj T*
(our policy proposal on advanced AI, the Advanced AI Framework \(AAIF\), we propose rules of the) Tj T*
(road for how any lab releases safe models, including transparency obligations that governments) Tj T*
(could require, such as risk reports. Together, these proposed measurements and policies are a) Tj T*
(starting point for monitoring the pace of AI development from outside the labs.) Tj T*
(\(1\) Measuring AI-led AI R&D) Tj T*
(Why measure AI-led R&D? Frontier AI labs increasingly use AI to build future AI models. This) Tj T*
(process allows labs in democratic countries to develop more capable models more quickly and) Tj T*
(conduct more safety and testing on models before they are released to secure AI's benefits) Tj T*
(while staying on the frontier. However, models accelerating their own development could make it) Tj T*
(more challenging for humans to understand or control these systems. It is therefore important) Tj T*
(to share these metrics to understand how close the world is to reaching recursive self) Tj T*
(improvement \(a model fully autonomously building its successor\).) Tj T*
(What we measured. We built a prototype index of how much of Anthropic's AI research and) Tj T*
(development \(R&D\) is performed by Claude, called the Anthropic R&D Automation Index. It's built) Tj T*
(by cataloguing every kind of AI R&D work done at the company, rating how automated each task) Tj T*
(currently is, and aggregating those ratings.) Tj T*
(What we found. To measure the extent to which AI is doing AI R&D at Anthropic, we use an) Tj T*
(automation rating scale developed by Epoch AI that measures "Automation Level," or AL. It runs) Tj T*
(from AL0 \(no AI involvement\) to AL5 \(AI operates fully autonomously, with no human in the) Tj T*
(loop\). In AL3, AI "collaborates": it can do large chunks of work under close human direction.) Tj T*
(In AL4, AI "leads": it can complete most of the task end-to-end from a high-level prompt, while) Tj T*
