(What any AI developer could report today. Any frontier developer could publish these measures) Tj T*
(regularly, using a public methodology. This would enable the numbers to be compared over time,) Tj T*
(and potentially across labs.) Tj T*
(Two obstacles stand in the way of cross-lab comparison on this type of reporting. First is the) Tj T*
(lack of a common methodology. Second, we're using our own models to evaluate our systems, which) Tj T*
(could mean that the "judge" model could make the same kinds of errors as the model it is) Tj T*
(checking. To address these challenges, a developer's measurements could be verified by a third) Tj T*
(party, or by other developers' models, with guardrails in place to limit the exchange of) Tj T*
(competitively sensitive data. These measures could also become the trigger for stronger) Tj T*
(requirements, like a fixed testing window before a new model is used for further AI R&D.) Tj T*
(\(2\) Measuring oversight of AI agents) Tj T*
(Why measure oversight of agents? Like other frontier developers, Anthropic employees) Tj T*
(increasingly delegate tasks to agents that work semi-autonomously for long stretches, and that) Tj T*
(delegate work to one another. As work becomes increasingly automated, from "AI collaborates") Tj T*
(toward "AI leads," agents could make more consequential decisions, such as which research) Tj T*
(direction to pursue next.) Tj T*
(These decisions need safeguards to block harmful behavior from an individual agent, as well as) Tj T*
(an oversight regime to detect problems that might only arise across many agents. In our) Tj T*
(monitoring data to date, individual agents rarely misbehave. But when there are millions or) Tj T*
(billions of agents operating in the economy, even rare events can happen regularly.) Tj T*
(What we measured. We've built a system that lets us oversee and intervene in actions AI agents) Tj T*
(take on Anthropic's systems. Here, we consider three different metrics: coverage, which) Tj T*
(describes the share of an agent's actions that pass through a monitor before or after) Tj T*
(execution; review latency, which is the time between an action and its review, first by an) Tj T*
(automated monitor and then by a human; and escalation rate, which is the share of agent) Tj T*
(activities that are either blocked/redirected \(in the case of online monitors\) or flagged for) Tj T*
(further review \(in the case of offline monitors\).) Tj T*
(What we found. As of August 2026, there were approximately 30,000 agents doing research and) Tj T*
(engineering work at Anthropic at any one time in our most-used internal platform. These) Tj T*
(measurements cover this platform only. The actions of these agents are constrained by two kinds) Tj T*
(of monitors, summarized below:) Tj T*
(Online monitorsOffline monitorsDescriptionOnline monitors check the actions of agents in real-) Tj T*
(time and either block dangerous actions or steer agent misbehavior automatically. They're built) Tj T*
(to address harms that would happen quickly and could not be undone, such as an agent copying) Tj T*
(model weights out of our systems.Offline monitors read agent activities after the fact. They) Tj T*
(are built to help address dangerous behaviors that develop slowly and can be reversed, like) Tj T*
(signs of model misalignment. We use flagged activities to improve our mitigations, like) Tj T*
(classifiers and deterministic controls. If the situation caused a large imminent danger, we) Tj T*
(would shut down the dangerous parts of the agent's deployment.Coverage100% of these agents') Tj T*
(actions pass through the online monitor before they are executed, usually within seconds.100%) Tj T*
(of these agents' actions are ingested by the monitor after they are taken.Review) Tj T*
(latencyAutomated review happens before an agent takes action; humans review any blocked actions) Tj T*
(within one week.The monitor flags roughly 100,000 transcripts per week that are then reviewed) Tj T*
(by multiple classifiers for false-positives and initial oversight review. Most of the flags are) Tj T*
(resolved by this process, and the highest priority flags \(approximately ~50 per week\) are) Tj T*
(escalated to human review.Blocking / escalation rateWe analyzed over a billion decisions from) Tj T*
(our research & engineering agents over August 2026 and found that 0.002% of them \(about 1 in) Tj T*
ET
