(What an AI developer could report today. Any developer running agents on its own research and) Tj T*
(engineering workloads could publish the same measures: coverage \(the share of agent activity) Tj T*
(that is monitored\), review latency \(how soon flagged activities are reviewed\), and escalation) Tj T*
(rate \(what share of agent activities the monitors block or flag\). Together, these measures) Tj T*
(would allow society to see whether oversight is keeping pace with the growing role of AI in AI) Tj T*
(R&D. We published all of these measurements in our recent risk report.) Tj T*
(Developers should share how often known agent misbehavior is caught by monitors, and should) Tj T*
(have third parties do this kind of testing independently. In the past, METR has independently) Tj T*
(red-teamed our offline monitoring platform. As described above, we are now setting up external) Tj T*
(third party evaluators at Anthropic.) Tj T*
(\(3\) Measuring compute allocation) Tj T*
(Why measure compute allocation? Broadly speaking, AI developers use compute for building more) Tj T*
(powerful models, serving customers, and safety-focused work like auditing a model's "thoughts",) Tj T*
(training model organisms to study misalignment, and evaluating whether a model can be safely) Tj T*
(deployed. Understanding how AI developers allocate their compute can tell you where a developer) Tj T*
(is focusing its resources and how that focus changes over time.) Tj T*
(Additionally, compute is among the most verifiable inputs to the AI R&D process, meaning that) Tj T*
(it could be a critical lever in a future pacing effort. A coordinated pacing effort could) Tj T*
(encourage companies to increase the compute allocated to safety across the industry and devote) Tj T*
(more resources to alignment, interpretability, safety testing, and evaluation.) Tj T*
(What we measured. We examined a snapshot of how Anthropic used all of its compute from July 13) Tj T*
(to July 20.2 To do that, we sorted every workload into a small number of categories, then asked) Tj T*
(how much of the compute going to AI R&D was safety work.) Tj T*
(Safety research tends to use less compute than frontier training runs by its nature, so compute) Tj T*
(is an imperfect proxy for how much a company focuses on safety. This is because safety research) Tj T*
(consists of individual researchers designing experiments, which is time-consuming even though) Tj T*
(running the experiments is not particularly compute-intensive. The value of this metric,) Tj T*
(therefore, is less the absolute numbers and more that it provides a straightforward mechanism) Tj T*
(to compare like with like, across developers and over time.) Tj T*
(What we found. Over the examined week, about 6% of compute that went to AI R&D was allocated) Tj T*
(toward safety, and about 12% of compute that went to AI-driven AI R&D was allocated toward) Tj T*
(safety.) Tj T*
(These are deliberately conservative estimates. For example, if a token was used to advance) Tj T*
(capabilities as much as it was to advance safety, it was not counted in these metrics.) Tj T*
(Additionally, these metrics do not account for safeguards classifiers, which are a separate,) Tj T*
(comparable amount of compute that make our models much safer for the world.) Tj T*
(What an AI developer could report today. Any frontier developer could publish what share of its) Tj T*
(AI R&D compute goes to safety work, with the category definitions published alongside and the) Tj T*
(classification checked by an independent third party.) Tj T*
(Safety research is hard to distinguish from capabilities research, and each developer will be) Tj T*
(tempted to draw the line generously. The burden of proof should sit with the developer to show) Tj T*
(that work is safety-related. Developers, governments, and the wider research community would) Tj T*
(benefit from converging on a shared definition ahead of time. A measurement like this could) Tj T*
(inform future actions, such as a lab's commitments about the share of compute going to safety) Tj T*
(research, or limits on the share of compute going towards AI research agents.) Tj T*
(Conclusion) Tj T*
(As the world considers pacing the frontier, we should do everything possible to minimize the) Tj T*
(gap between what frontier labs know and what the public knows. This means better measuring the) Tj T*
(development of AI, reporting on it publicly, and giving society an opportunity to decide how to) Tj T*
(use this information. We hope to model that transparency by releasing these measurements, and) Tj T*
ET
endstream
