(Nevertheless, we plan to rebuild the basket of tasks periodically and re-version our published) Tj T*
(automation numbers as appropriate.) Tj T*
(Oversight of agents) Tj T*
(How we did it. In our most commonly used internal agent scaffold, two design choices allow us) Tj T*
(to more easily detect unknown unknowns and let agents monitor each other:) Tj T*
(Identity. Most AI users are accustomed to talking to a single "Claude" across many different) Tj T*
(chats. With many agents working together, we have found it important to give agents an) Tj T*
(individual identity, and tie all of the data that agent creates to its identity. This lets an) Tj T*
(agent distinguish itself from others, and treat what comes from another agent as a claim to) Tj T*
(check rather than a thought of its own. It reduces the risk of correlated actions, by allowing) Tj T*
(agents to make judgments based on their individual experience. And because the identity is not) Tj T*
(tied to a model, it persists through model upgrades, so an agent's record is continuous even if) Tj T*
(the underlying model powering it changes. From an oversight perspective, this design ensures) Tj T*
(that every action can be audited per agent across time, and that every data record can be) Tj T*
(linked back to a specific agent.) Tj T*
(Open communication. Agents communicate through a shared, open messaging system, rather than) Tj T*
(privately. Every message is tied to the identity of the agent that posted it and can link to) Tj T*
(other content, so that the agents are sharing original references. This allows agents to avoid) Tj T*
("playing telephone" as they communicate. Because agents can see each others' messages, they can) Tj T*
(correct each others' errors, and coordinate about shared work. All messages are cross-) Tj T*
(referenced with agent transcripts, allowing behavioral monitoring to traverse communication) Tj T*
(between agents.) Tj T*
(What this does and doesn't capture. At this scale of agent activity, it is hard to be certain) Tj T*
(we have a complete picture of all possible kinds of behaviors, or that we are making these) Tj T*
(patterns adequately legible to human oversight. We have been doing this kind of monitoring for) Tj T*
(months, not years, and expect the science of agent monitoring to change considerably going) Tj T*
(forward.) Tj T*
(Measuring compute allocation) Tj T*
(How we did it. We started with our existing compute monitoring tools; Anthropic, like) Tj T*
(presumably every frontier developer, has several monitoring tools built for capacity planning) Tj T*
(that periodically sample accelerator usage and tag workloads with best-efforts labels \(i.e.,) Tj T*
(research and model development, internal usage, first-party inference, and so on\) based on its) Tj T*
(metadata. Usage on third-party cloud compute is reported to us by the providers and folded in.) Tj T*
(Most of the work of this exercise was stitching these existing sources together.) Tj T*
(We then used Claude to classify each workload as either safety work or AI R&D via a prompted) Tj T*
(classifier. Safety work was defined as work whose dominant purpose is making AI systems safer,) Tj T*
(more understandable, or more secure. Everything else, including capability research, training) Tj T*
(production models, product development, and developer tooling, was counted as AI R&D. Work that) Tj T*
(helps capability as much as it helps safety was also counted as AI R&D, so the safety share is) Tj T*
(conservative.) Tj T*
(For research training and evaluation runs, we built a classifier that reads the run's metadata) Tj T*
(and the code it used, and returns a classification, a justification, and a confidence level.) Tj T*
(Rather than classify all of the week's almost 10,000 runs, we sampled about 14% of them,) Tj T*
(weighting the sample toward the runs that used the most compute, so that the result reflects) Tj T*
(where the compute actually went, rather than how many runs there were. For inference for AI) Tj T*
(research agents, a variant of the same classifier read the agent's session transcript. Where) Tj T*
(transcripts were inaccessible \(usually due to the work being compartmentalized\), we classified) Tj T*
(them by the user's team or conservatively defaulted to classifying them as AI R&D. We plan to) Tj T*
(refine this pipeline so that an independent third-party could re-run the classifier on a random) Tj T*
(subsample of jobs and transcripts and check both the sorting and the totals.) Tj T*
(You're helping to perform an internal audit at the frontier AI company Anthropic to track where) Tj T*
(our research compute goes. The aim of the audit is to produce a public-facing breakdown of the) Tj T*
ET
endstream
