(What this does and doesn't capture. The main lesson of this exercise is that classifying what) Tj T*
(is and isn't safety work is difficult but tractable, since the boundary between these) Tj T*
(categories is not black and white. For example, research on scalable oversight might make) Tj T*
(future models more aligned and current models more commercially useful  -  it's difficult to) Tj T*
(determine whether this is primarily safety- or capabilities-advancing. We found that an) Tj T*
(extensive written definition of each task, with clear boundary cases \(an excerpt is above\),) Tj T*
(gets the classifier to agree with human reviewers within one or two percentage points of) Tj T*
(difference between the human and machine raters. But some cases were too difficult to determine) Tj T*
(even after several hours of human review. Our definition is one reasonable choice among many; a) Tj T*
(different developer, or a regulator, might draw the line differently.) Tj T*
(Three further limitations matter. First, many of the underlying labels we relied on \(i.e.,) Tj T*
(reasons for runs, workload tags, the source of API traffic\) are set by automated rules, or) Tj T*
(occasionally directly by users, and are best-effort, not verified. In most cases, we expect) Tj T*
(that our classifications are accurate, but in some cases usage may be mislabeled and our) Tj T*
(pipeline would not necessarily catch it. A measurement meant to be trusted by outsiders will) Tj T*
(need to be complete, accurate, and technically enforced. Second, the measurement covers one) Tj T*
(week, which is enough to show that the measurement can be made, but not enough to show a) Tj T*
(meaningful trend. Third, and most importantly, compute share measures only what is spent. A) Tj T*
(more efficient safety classifier, or a faster inference stack for production models, lowers the) Tj T*
(safety portion, but doesn't mean we're doing less safety work. Our own classifier overheads) Tj T*
(have fallen with efficiency improvements, and have risen when production inference was more) Tj T*
(efficient than the classifiers were.) Tj T*
